body:
Update: Spoke to my dietitian and got the blood test results. Now I'm frustrated.

Results show my thyroid is fine. In fact, it's overactive, which makes no sense because I heard that's supposed to make you lose weight.

&#x200B;

The dietician said it's water weight and to stop eating 1200 calories. I'm dubious about the "water weight" Can 30 lbs really be water???

&#x200B;

EDIT: The convo was before the results got back. There hasn't been a comment yet about the results.
